                        "cot": "\n\nC) Various types of animals produce pollen and seeds.\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- Pollen and seeds are reproductive structures of plants.\n- Plants need to reproduce to ensure the survival of their species.\n- Pollination is the process by which pollen is transferred from the male part of a plant to the female part, leading to fertilization and the production of seeds.\n- While some plants rely on wind or water to spread their pollen, many others depend on animals to carry it from one flower to another.\n- Animals that help with pollination include bees, butterflies, moths, birds, bats, and even some mammals like rodents and primates.\n- When an animal visits a flower to feed on its nectar or pollen, some of the pollen sticks to its body and is carried to the next flower it visits, where it may fertilize the ovules and produce seeds.\n- Therefore, various types of animals produce pollen and seeds by acting as pollinators for plants.",
