                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Chlorine is commonly used to disinfect water and kill harmful bacteria and viruses. However, too much chlorine can be harmful to human health.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. How much chlorine was added to the water?\n2. Has the chlorine had enough time to dissipate?\n3. What are the potential health risks of drinking chlorine water?\n\nAnswering sub-questions:\n1. The amount of chlorine added to the water is important because too much chlorine can be harmful to human health. If the water has been treated with a safe amount of chlorine, it may be safe to drink.\n2. If the chlorine has had enough time to dissipate, it may be safe to drink. However, the amount of time required for chlorine to dissipate depends on various factors such as temperature, sunlight exposure, and the amount of chlorine added to the water.\n3. The potential health risks of drinking chlorine water include nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, and stomach cramps. In severe cases, it can lead to respiratory problems, eye irritation, and skin irritation.\n\nAnswer: Based on the sub-questions, it is difficult to determine whether week old chlorine water is safe to drink without additional information. It is important to know how much chlorine was added to the water and whether it has had enough time to dissipate. If the water has been treated with a safe amount of chlorine and has had enough time to dissipate, it may be safe to drink. However, there are potential health risks associated with drinking chlorine water, especially if it has been sitting for a week. Therefore, it is recommended to consult with a water treatment professional or a healthcare provider before drinking week old chlorine water. The answer is neither true nor false.",
