                        "cot": "Rephrased question: Was the construction of the Great Pyramids carried out by a government with religious leaders in charge?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- The Great Pyramids are located in Egypt.\n- Ancient Egypt was ruled by pharaohs who were considered divine beings.\n- The pharaohs had a theocratic government, meaning that religious leaders held significant power and influence.\n- The construction of the Great Pyramids was a massive undertaking that required a large workforce and extensive resources.\n- It is likely that the theocratic government played a role in organizing and overseeing the construction of the pyramids.\n\nAnswer: A) True, the Great Pyramids were likely built by a theocratic government.",
