                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I have a question. If someone is lactose intolerant, do they have to avoid cream?\n\nProfessor: That's a good question. The answer is true, they should avoid cream.\n\nStudent: Why is that, Professor?\n\nProfessor: Cream is a dairy product and contains lactose, which is a type of sugar found in milk. People who are lactose intolerant have difficulty digesting lactose, which can cause symptoms such as bloating, gas, and diarrhea.\n\nStudent: So, if someone is lactose intolerant, can they have any dairy products at all?\n\nProfessor: It depends on the individual and the severity of their lactose intolerance. Some people may be able to tolerate small amounts of dairy, while others may need to avoid it completely. There are also lactose-free dairy products available, such as lactose-free milk and cheese.\n\nStudent: How can someone know if they are lactose intolerant?\n\nProfessor: The most common way to diagnose lactose intolerance is through a lactose tolerance test. This involves drinking a liquid that contains lactose and then measuring the amount of glucose in the blood over time. If the body has difficulty digesting lactose, the glucose levels will not rise as they should.\n\nStudent: Thank you for explaining that, Professor. It makes sense now why someone who is lactose intolerant should avoid cream.",
