                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: What are yin and yang colors?\nYin and yang are concepts from Chinese philosophy that represent opposite but complementary forces. In terms of colors, yin colors are cool and calming, such as blue and green, while yang colors are warm and energizing, such as red and orange.\n\nStep 2: What are rainbows?\nRainbows are optical phenomena that occur when sunlight is refracted, or bent, by water droplets in the air. This causes the light to separate into its component colors, which are then visible as a spectrum of colors in the sky.\n\nStep 3: Can rainbows be made by mixing yin and yang colors?\nNo, rainbows are not made by mixing colors at all. They are a natural phenomenon caused by the refraction of light. While the colors of the rainbow can be described in terms of yin and yang (with blue and green being yin and red and orange being yang), this has nothing to do with how rainbows are formed.\n\nAnswer: B) False",
