                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Blue lips can be a sign of a medical condition or a symptom of exposure to cold temperatures.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What causes lips to turn blue?\n2. Is it normal for lips to turn blue in certain situations?\n3. When is blue lips a cause for concern?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Lips turn blue when there is a lack of oxygen in the blood. This can be caused by a variety of medical conditions, such as asthma, pneumonia, or heart disease. It can also be a symptom of exposure to cold temperatures.\n2. It is normal for lips to turn blue in certain situations, such as when exposed to cold temperatures or during high altitude activities. In these cases, the blue color should go away once the person warms up or returns to a lower altitude.\n3. Blue lips are a cause for concern when they are accompanied by other symptoms, such as shortness of breath, chest pain, or confusion. If someone's lips are consistently blue, it is important to seek medical attention to determine the underlying cause.",
