                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Kidney is a type of organ meat that is commonly consumed in many cultures. It is a good source of protein, vitamins, and minerals, but it also contains high levels of certain substances that can be harmful if consumed in excess.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are the potential health risks associated with eating kidney?\n2. How much kidney can be safely consumed?\n3. What are the benefits of eating kidney?\n\nAnswering sub-question 1: \nKidney contains high levels of purines, which can be converted into uric acid in the body. Excessive consumption of purine-rich foods can lead to the formation of uric acid crystals, which can cause gout and kidney stones. Kidney also contains high levels of vitamin A, which can be toxic in large amounts and cause symptoms such as nausea, dizziness, and headaches.\n\nAnswering sub-question 2:\nThe amount of kidney that can be safely consumed depends on various factors such as age, sex, weight, and overall health. In general, it is recommended to limit the consumption of organ meats to once or twice a week and to avoid eating large amounts in one sitting. It is also important to cook kidney thoroughly to reduce the risk of bacterial contamination.\n\nAnswering sub-question 3:\nKidney is a good source of protein, iron, zinc, and vitamin B12. It is also low in fat and calories, making it a healthy choice for people who are trying to lose weight or maintain a healthy diet. However, it is important to balance the benefits of eating kidney with the potential health risks and to consume it in moderation. \n\nAnswering the original question:\nBased on the information provided, the answer to the question \"Is it safe to eat kidney?\" is: B) False. While kidney can be a healthy and nutritious food, it also contains high levels of purines and vitamin A, which can be harmful if consumed in excess. It is important to limit the consumption of kidney and to cook it thoroughly to reduce the risk of health problems.",
