                        "id": "bafbe29b-656e-4139-8750-cf62e88d69cd",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " Embalming is a process of preserving a body after death. It involves draining the body of fluids and replacing them with a mixture of chemicals to slow down the decomposition process. During the embalming process, the body is often posed in a lifelike position and the face is made up to look more natural.\n\nAt a funeral, the embalmed body will look and feel different than it did in life. It will be cold to the touch and may feel stiff or rigid. The body may also have a waxy or plastic-like texture. The face may look different due to the makeup and the body may be posed in a different position.",
