                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nAs an AI language model, I can provide an answer based on scientific evidence and research. Gorillas and humans are both primates, which means they share a common ancestor. However, the degree of relatedness between the two species depends on how closely related they are in terms of their genetic makeup. \n\nTo determine the genetic relatedness between gorillas and humans, scientists have conducted various studies, including DNA sequencing and comparative genomics. These studies have shown that humans and gorillas share about 98% of their DNA, which indicates a high degree of genetic similarity. \n\nFurthermore, both humans and gorillas have similar physical characteristics, such as opposable thumbs, forward-facing eyes, and large brains. These similarities suggest that humans and gorillas have evolved from a common ancestor and share a close evolutionary relationship. \n\nTherefore, based on scientific evidence, it can be concluded that gorillas are closely related to humans. The answer is A) True.",
