                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain if gorillas are closely related to humans?\n\nProfessor: Yes, of course. The answer is true. Gorillas are closely related to humans.\n\nStudent: How are they related?\n\nProfessor: Gorillas and humans are both primates, which means we share a common ancestor. Our DNA is also very similar, with about 98% of our DNA being identical.\n\nStudent: So, does that mean gorillas are our closest relatives?\n\nProfessor: No, chimpanzees are actually our closest relatives. However, gorillas are still very closely related to us.\n\nStudent: How did scientists figure out that gorillas are closely related to humans?\n\nProfessor: Scientists have studied the DNA of many different species and have found that the more similar the DNA is, the more closely related the species are. They have also studied the physical characteristics and behavior of gorillas and humans and have found many similarities.\n\nStudent: Thank you, Professor. I understand now that gorillas are closely related to humans because we share a common ancestor and have similar DNA and physical characteristics.",
