                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The Moon is a natural satellite of Earth and orbits around it. It takes approximately 27.3 days for the Moon to complete one orbit around Earth.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the definition of \"once per day\"?\n- \"Once per day\" means an event that happens every 24 hours.\n\n2. Does the Moon rise once per day?\n- Yes, the Moon rises once per day. This is because the Moon orbits around Earth and as Earth rotates on its axis, the Moon appears to rise in the east and set in the west once every 24 hours.\n\n3. Does the new Moon occur once per day?\n- No, the new Moon does not occur once per day. The new Moon occurs when the Moon is between the Sun and Earth, and the side of the Moon facing Earth is not illuminated by the Sun. This happens approximately once every 29.5 days.\n\n4. Does the Moon cycle through its phases once per day?\n- No, the Moon does not cycle through its phases once per day. The Moon's phases are caused by the changing angle between the Sun, Earth, and Moon, and it takes approximately 29.5 days for the Moon to cycle through its phases.\n\n5. Does the Moon pass in front of the Sun once per day?\n- No, the Moon does not pass in front of the Sun once per day. A solar eclipse occurs when the Moon passes between the Sun and Earth, but this happens only a few times per year and is not a daily occurrence.\n\nAnswer: The event that occurs once per day is the Moon rising. Therefore, the correct answer is A) The Moon rises.",
