                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What is a true statement about the arrangement of planets in the solar system?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- Option A states that gas planets are closer to the Sun. This is not true as the four inner planets (Mercury, Venus, Earth, and Mars) are solid and closer to the Sun than the four outer gas planets (Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, and Neptune).\n- Option B states that solid planets are closer to the Sun. This is true as explained above.\n- Option C states that the planets are arranged in order of increasing size. This is not true as the order of the planets from the Sun is: Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, and Neptune. The sizes of the planets do not follow this order.\n- Option D states that solid planets are much larger than gas planets. This is not true as the gas planets are much larger than the solid planets.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) The solid planets are closer to the Sun.",
