                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The solar system consists of eight planets, including Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, and Neptune. The four inner planets are solid and rocky, while the four outer planets are gas giants. The planets are arranged in order of increasing distance from the Sun.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are the four inner planets made of?\n2. What are the four outer planets made of?\n3. How are the planets arranged in the solar system?\n4. Is there a correlation between a planet's distance from the Sun and its composition?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The four inner planets (Mercury, Venus, Earth, and Mars) are solid and rocky.\n2. The four outer planets (Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, and Neptune) are gas giants.\n3. The planets are arranged in order of increasing distance from the Sun: Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, and Neptune.\n4. Yes, there is a correlation between a planet's distance from the Sun and its composition. The inner planets are closer to the Sun and are made of solid, rocky material, while the outer planets are farther from the Sun and are made of gas and ice. Therefore, statement B is true: the solid planets are closer to the Sun.",
