                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "D) the Moon to appear as different shapes during the month.\n\nThe Moon's revolution around Earth causes it to move in an elliptical orbit, which means that its distance from Earth changes throughout the month. As the Moon moves farther away from Earth, it appears smaller and less bright, while when it is closer, it appears larger and brighter. Additionally, the angle at which the Sun's light hits the Moon changes as it moves around Earth, causing different parts of the Moon to be illuminated and creating the different shapes we see during the month, known as the phases of the Moon. Therefore, the correct answer is D) the Moon to appear as different shapes during the month.",
