                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: Which of the following actions is an example of gravity affecting other systems?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\nA) Surface water evaporating into the atmosphere: This is not an example of gravity affecting other systems. The process of evaporation is driven by heat energy, not gravity.\n\nB) Planets moving around the Sun in an elliptical pattern: This is an example of gravity affecting other systems. The gravitational force of the Sun is what keeps the planets in their orbits.\n\nC) Glaciers melting because of increasing temperatures: This is not an example of gravity affecting other systems. The melting of glaciers is caused by rising temperatures, not gravity.\n\nD) Groundwater moving to the surface in an artesian well: This is not an example of gravity affecting other systems. The movement of groundwater in an artesian well is caused by pressure differences, not gravity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) planets moving around the Sun in an elliptical pattern.",
