                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Gravity is a force of attraction between objects. It is responsible for keeping planets in orbit around the Sun and for keeping objects on Earth's surface. \n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is surface water?\n2. How does gravity affect surface water?\n3. What is the process of evaporation?\n4. How does gravity influence the process of evaporation?\n5. What is the relationship between planets and the Sun?\n6. How does gravity affect the movement of planets?\n7. What are glaciers?\n8. How do increasing temperatures affect glaciers?\n9. What is an artesian well?\n10. How does gravity influence the movement of groundwater in an artesian well?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Surface water is water that is on the Earth's surface, such as in lakes, rivers, and oceans.\n2. Gravity affects surface water by pulling it towards the center of the Earth, causing it to flow downhill and eventually reach the ocean.\n3. Evaporation is the process by which a liquid, such as water, turns into a gas, such as water vapor.\n4. Gravity influences the process of evaporation by pulling the water vapor towards the Earth's surface, where it can condense and form clouds.\n5. Planets are celestial bodies that orbit around a star, such as the Sun.\n6. Gravity affects the movement of planets by pulling them towards the Sun and keeping them in orbit around it.\n7. Glaciers are large masses of ice that form on land and move slowly downhill due to gravity.\n8. Increasing temperatures can cause glaciers to melt, which can lead to rising sea levels and changes in the Earth's climate.\n9. An artesian well is a well that taps into a confined aquifer, where the water is under pressure and can flow to the surface without the need for a pump.\n10. Gravity influences the movement of groundwater in an artesian well by pulling the water towards the surface and allowing it to flow out of the well. \n\nAnswer: B) planets moving around the Sun in an elliptical pattern is an example of gravity influencing other systems.",
                        "answers": [
