                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we know that dinosaurs lived millions of years ago. This means that they are extinct and no longer exist today. \n\nNext, we need to think about where fossils are typically found. Fossils are the preserved remains or traces of organisms from the past, and they are usually found in sedimentary rocks. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) rocks in the ground. Fossils of dinosaurs have been found all over the world in various types of sedimentary rocks, such as sandstone, shale, and limestone. They are often discovered during excavations or construction projects, and paleontologists study them to learn more about the history of life on Earth.",
                        "answers": [
