                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nD) rocks in the ground.\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- Dinosaurs are extinct animals that lived millions of years ago.\n- When an animal dies, its body may be buried by sediment (such as sand, mud, or volcanic ash) over time.\n- The sediment can harden into rock, preserving the remains of the animal as a fossil.\n- Therefore, the fossils of dinosaurs are most commonly found in rocks in the ground, such as sedimentary rocks like sandstone, shale, or limestone.\n- Fossils can also be found in other types of rocks, such as volcanic or metamorphic rocks, but these are less common for dinosaur fossils.\n- Dinosaurs did not live in water or ice, so their fossils are not likely to be found in those environments.\n- Similarly, dinosaurs did not climb trees or live inside them, so their fossils are not likely to be found in the trunks of trees.",
