                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Think about where dinosaurs lived and died.\n2. Consider how fossils are formed.\n3. Determine which of the options listed would be the most likely place for dinosaur fossils to be found based on steps 1 and 2.\n\nAnswer: D) rocks in the ground. \n\nExplanation: Dinosaurs lived on land, so it is unlikely that their fossils would be found in the water of oceans or the ice on ponds. Fossils are formed when the remains of plants and animals are buried in sediment and over time, the minerals in the sediment replace the organic material, creating a fossil. This process is most likely to occur in sedimentary rocks, which are formed from layers of sediment. Therefore, the most likely place to find dinosaur fossils is in rocks in the ground.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "87ad9c4f-25d2-474c-991f-22cbbaa0930f",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) rocks in the ground.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "D",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/03/30 00:19:47",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
                        "model": "{'name': 'gpt-3.5-turbo', 'temperature': 0, 'max_tokens': 512}",
