                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is D) rocks in the ground.\n\nTo arrive at this answer, we need to consider the geological processes that occur over millions of years. When a dinosaur dies, its body may be buried by sediment such as sand or mud. Over time, more layers of sediment accumulate on top, and the weight of these layers compresses the lower layers into rock. The dinosaur's bones may also be replaced by minerals, a process called fossilization. \n\nTherefore, the fossils of dinosaurs are typically found in rocks in the ground. While it is possible for fossils to be found in other locations such as the water of oceans or the ice on ponds, these are much less common and usually require specific conditions to preserve the fossils. The trunks of trees are also an unlikely location for dinosaur fossils, as trees typically do not grow in the same environments where dinosaurs lived and died.",
                        "answers": [
