                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: Where can the fossils of dinosaurs that lived millions of years ago be found?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- Dinosaurs lived millions of years ago and are now extinct.\n- Fossils are the remains or traces of ancient organisms that have been preserved in rocks or sediments.\n- Therefore, to find the fossils of dinosaurs, we need to look for rocks or sediments that are millions of years old.\n- Option A, the water of oceans, is unlikely to preserve fossils for millions of years because of the constant movement and erosion of water.\n- Option B, the ice on ponds, is also unlikely to preserve fossils for millions of years because ice is a relatively recent geological feature and can melt or shift easily.\n- Option C, the trunks of trees, is not a typical place to find dinosaur fossils because trees are not usually associated with the habitats of dinosaurs.\n- Option D, rocks in the ground, is the most likely place to find dinosaur fossils because rocks can preserve fossils for millions of years and are often associated with the geological formations where dinosaurs lived.\n\nAnswer: D) rocks in the ground.",
