                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what is meant by \"extensive glaciation\" in this context?\n\nProfessor: Sure, extensive glaciation refers to a period of time when large areas of land were covered by ice sheets and glaciers.\n\nStudent: How could extensive glaciation disrupt ocean ecosystems?\n\nProfessor: Glaciers can cause a steep drop in ocean salinity and density. As glaciers melt, they release fresh water into the ocean, which dilutes the saltwater and reduces its density. This can disrupt the ocean's circulation patterns and affect the distribution of nutrients and oxygen.\n\nStudent: So, which effect is the correct answer?\n\nProfessor: The correct answer is A) steep drop in ocean salinity and density. This can have a significant impact on ocean ecosystems and could potentially lead to extinctions.\n\nStudent: Can you explain why the other options are not correct?\n\nProfessor: Option B) steep drop in ocean volume and area is not correct because glaciers do not directly affect the volume or area of the ocean. Option C) increased exposure of oceans to ultraviolet radiation is not correct because glaciers do not have any direct impact on the amount of ultraviolet radiation that reaches the ocean. Option D) increased exposure of tsunamis to ocean life is not correct because glaciers do not have any direct impact on the frequency or intensity of tsunamis.",
