                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nA) Spreading plant and animal life over a wider area: While ocean currents can transport organisms, this is not their primary function in affecting world climate. This option is incorrect.\n\nB) Ensuring ocean density is not the same globally: Ocean currents do play a role in maintaining differences in ocean density, but this is not their primary function in affecting world climate. This option is incorrect.\n\nC) Carrying sediment from rivers and inland basins: While ocean currents can transport sediment, this is not their primary function in affecting world climate. This option is incorrect.\n\nD) Transferring heat to and from various regions: This is the correct answer. Ocean currents play a crucial role in transferring heat from one region to another, which affects global climate patterns. For example, the Gulf Stream carries warm water from the Gulf of Mexico to the North Atlantic, which helps to moderate temperatures in Europe. Similarly, the cold water currents in the Pacific Ocean help to cool the western coast of South America. Therefore, option D is the correct answer.",
