                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Ocean currents are large-scale movements of water in the ocean that are driven by a combination of factors, including wind, temperature, and salinity. The Gulf Stream is a warm ocean current that originates in the Gulf of Mexico and flows northeastward along the eastern coast of the United States before turning eastward across the Atlantic Ocean.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the Gulf Stream?\n2. How does the Gulf Stream affect world climate?\n3. What factors drive ocean currents?\n4. How do ocean currents affect plant and animal life?\n5. How does the Gulf Stream affect ocean density?\n6. How do ocean currents transport sediment?\n7. How do ocean currents transfer heat?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The Gulf Stream is a warm ocean current that originates in the Gulf of Mexico and flows northeastward along the eastern coast of the United States before turning eastward across the Atlantic Ocean.\n2. The Gulf Stream affects world climate by transferring heat from the tropics to higher latitudes, which helps to moderate temperatures in regions like western Europe. It also affects weather patterns and can influence the distribution of precipitation.\n3. Ocean currents are driven by a combination of factors, including wind, temperature, and salinity. The Gulf Stream is primarily driven by the rotation of the Earth and the prevailing winds in the North Atlantic.\n4. Ocean currents can affect the distribution of plant and animal life by carrying nutrients and other materials to different regions. The Gulf Stream, for example, helps to support a diverse array of marine life along the eastern coast of the United States and in the North Atlantic.\n5. Ocean density is not the same globally because of differences in temperature and salinity. The Gulf Stream, which is warm and salty, helps to maintain a higher density of water in the North Atlantic compared to other regions.\n6. Ocean currents can transport sediment from rivers and inland basins to the ocean, where it can be deposited on the seafloor or carried to other regions. The Gulf Stream can transport sediment from the eastern coast of the United States to the North Atlantic.\n7. Ocean currents transfer heat from warmer regions to cooler regions, which helps to regulate global temperatures. The Gulf Stream, for example, transfers heat from the tropics to higher latitudes, which helps to moderate temperatures in regions like western Europe.",
                        "answers": [
