                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The Northern Hemisphere includes North America, Europe, Asia, and parts of Africa. June to November is the Atlantic hurricane season.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are the major natural disasters that can occur in the Northern Hemisphere?\n2. What are the common months for hurricanes in the Northern Hemisphere?\n3. Are there any potential asteroid impacts predicted for the Northern Hemisphere during this time period?\n4. Are there any active volcanoes in the Northern Hemisphere that could potentially erupt during this time period?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The major natural disasters that can occur in the Northern Hemisphere include hurricanes, earthquakes, tsunamis, volcanic eruptions, and wildfires.\n2. The common months for hurricanes in the Northern Hemisphere are June to November, with the peak season being from August to October.\n3. There are no known potential asteroid impacts predicted for the Northern Hemisphere during this time period.\n4. There are several active volcanoes in the Northern Hemisphere that could potentially erupt during this time period, including Mount St. Helens in the United States, Mount Etna in Italy, and Mount Fuji in Japan. However, it is difficult to predict when a volcano will erupt.",
