                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What type of energy transformation most likely occurred when a student's breakfast provided energy for bicycling later in the day?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- The breakfast provided energy to the student's body.\n- This energy was then used to power the student's muscles during bicycling.\n- Therefore, the energy transformation must involve the conversion of the breakfast's energy into the energy used by the muscles.\n- The breakfast likely contained chemical energy (from food molecules).\n- The energy used by the muscles is mechanical energy (movement).\n- Therefore, the most likely energy transformation is from chemical to mechanical energy.\n\nAnswer: D) chemical to mechanical.",
