                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) tidal energy and hydropower\n\nExplanation:\n- Gravitational energy is the potential energy stored in an object due to its position in a gravitational field. \n- Tidal energy is generated by the gravitational pull of the moon and the sun on the Earth's oceans, causing tides to rise and fall. This movement of water can be harnessed to generate electricity through the use of turbines. \n- Hydropower is generated by the gravitational force of falling water, which turns turbines to generate electricity. \n- Geothermal energy is generated by the heat from the Earth's core, and wind energy is generated by the movement of air currents. Neither of these sources use gravitational energy to generate electricity. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) tidal energy and hydropower.",
