                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What are the alternative energy resources that generate electricity using gravitational energy?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- Gravitational energy is the potential energy stored in an object due to its position in a gravitational field.\n- To generate electricity from gravitational energy, we need to convert this potential energy into kinetic energy, which can then be used to turn a turbine and generate electricity.\n- Tidal energy and hydropower are two alternative energy resources that use the gravitational energy of water to generate electricity.\n- Tidal energy harnesses the gravitational pull of the moon and the sun on the Earth's oceans to create tidal currents that can be used to turn turbines.\n- Hydropower uses the gravitational energy of falling water to turn turbines and generate electricity.\n- Geothermal energy and wind energy do not use gravitational energy to generate electricity.\n- Geothermal energy harnesses the heat energy from the Earth's core to generate electricity.\n- Wind energy uses the kinetic energy of wind to turn turbines and generate electricity.\n- Therefore, the answer is A) tidal energy and hydropower.\n\nAnswer: A) tidal energy and hydropower.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "253a46eb-2caf-42c1-84a2-1285ac579ac4",
