                    {
                        "id": "e6e11432-40b5-4ed6-ac6f-1129cb856fbf",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Gravitational energy is the potential energy stored in an object due to its position in a gravitational field.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is tidal energy?\n2. How does tidal energy use gravitational energy to make electricity?\n3. What is hydropower?\n4. How does hydropower use gravitational energy to make electricity?\n5. What is geothermal energy?\n6. How does geothermal energy generate electricity?\n7. What is wind energy?\n8. How does wind energy generate electricity?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Tidal energy is a form of renewable energy that harnesses the power of the tides to generate electricity.\n2. Tidal energy uses the gravitational pull of the moon and the sun to create tidal movements in the ocean, which are then captured by turbines to generate electricity.\n3. Hydropower is a form of renewable energy that uses the gravitational energy of falling water to generate electricity.\n4. Hydropower plants use dams to store water at a higher elevation, which creates potential energy. When the water is released, it flows downhill and turns turbines to generate electricity.\n5. Geothermal energy is a form of renewable energy that harnesses the heat from the Earth's core to generate electricity.\n6. Geothermal power plants use the natural heat of the Earth to create steam, which drives turbines to generate electricity.\n7. Wind energy is a form of renewable energy that uses the kinetic energy of wind to generate electricity.\n8. Wind turbines capture the kinetic energy of the wind and convert it into electricity through the rotation of the blades, which turn a generator. \n\nAnswer: A) tidal energy and hydropower use gravitational energy to make electricity.",
                        "answers": [
