                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What happens to light when it hits a mirror?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- Light is a form of electromagnetic radiation that travels in straight lines.\n- When light hits a surface, it can be either absorbed, transmitted, refracted, or reflected.\n- Refraction occurs when light passes through a medium with a different density, causing it to change direction.\n- Transmission occurs when light passes through a transparent or translucent material without being absorbed or reflected.\n- Absorption occurs when light is absorbed by a material, converting its energy into heat or other forms of energy.\n- Reflection occurs when light bounces off a surface, changing its direction but not its wavelength.\n\nTherefore, when light hits a mirror, most of the light is reflected.\n\nAnswer: B) Reflected.",
